      "writtenOn": "2021-09-02T07:16:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That exact topic is discussed in parent CL crrev/c/2420477 regarding \"nonatomic handling of register\".\n\n\u003e https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2420477/11/driver/tcpm/tcpci.c#1253\n\nThis non-atomicity is what I suggested deferring on for now. Hence split this CL off to be the most non-invasive mitigation.\n\nI do not believe a formal bug has been filed regarding ALERT register handling. I have not filed one since current code is sensitive to ordering, and doesn\u0027t exploit necessary features of TCPCI spec to handle ALERT registers asynchronously. For example: Extended Alerts (FRS) would need to be re-ordered to be handled first, in order to not block de-asserting ALERT# line due to Standard Alert register. Long I2C RX_BUF accesses would need to be interrupted on FRS ALERT. Etc.\n\nAnother example: we don\u0027t (currently) handle MessageID repeats /before/ packet queue. Working Groups have advised handling it there; in the interrupt handler. Such changes would be too major for this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "0dfe8195_b35676cd",
      "revId": "8c094dfd9a65ade715a52cfec25761e0f7e124ee",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
